<title>SINGAPORE: Sime Singapore first half net surges.</title>
<headline>Sime Singapore first half net surges.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1997-03-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Six months to December 31, 1996 (in millions of S$ unless stated)</p>
<p>    Net profit			     17.4  vs  5.1</p>
<p>    Dividend (cents)			1.25 vs  1.00</p>
<p>    Group shr (cents)		     3.20 vs  0.90</p>
<p>    Turnover				338.5  vs  293.1</p>
<p>    Interest income			 0.2  vs    0.1</p>
<p>    Interest (expense)		    1.5  vs    1.5</p>
<p>    Depreciation (expense)		6.8  vs    6.0</p>
<p>    Profits from associates	     4.0  vs    4.5</p>
<p>    Pre-tax profit			 24.9  vs   11.7</p>
<p>    Tax					 6.8  vs    6.0</p>
<p>    Minorities		     (loss) 0.7  vs    0.6  (loss)</p>
<p>Dividend pay date: May 28 1997</p>
<p>Last day books open: May 20 1997  </p>
<p>Note - Sime Singapore Ltd is a diversified conglomerate involved in consumer services, engineering, heavy equipment, insurance, motor dealerships, packaging and property. It is a unit of Malaysia's Sime Darby Bhd.</p>
<p>-- Singapore newsroom (65 8703199)</p>
</text>
